\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. That mystic Word of Thine,
\par O sovereign Lord,
\par Is all too pure, too high, too 
\par deep for me;
\par Weary of striving, and with
\par longing faint,
\par I breathe it back again in prayer to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Abide in me, I pray, and I in Thee;
\par From this good hour, O leave 
\par me nevermore!
\par Then shall the discord cease, the 
\par wound be healed,
\par The life-long bleeding of the soul
\par be o'er.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Abide in me; o'ershadow by Thy love
\par Each half-formed purpose and 
\par dark thought of sin;
\par Quench, ere it rise, each selfish,
\par low desire;
\par And keep my soul as Thine, 
\par calm and divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. As some rare perfume in a vase
\par of clay
\par Pervades it with a fragrance not its own,
\par So, when 
\par Thou dwellest in a mortal soul,
\par All heaven's own sweetness seems
\par around it thrown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Abide in me: there have been
\par moments blest
\par When I have heard Thy voice and felt
\par Thy power:
\par Then evil lost its grasp, and passion, hushed,
\par Owned the Divine enchantment
\par of the hour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. These were but seasons beautiful
\par and rare,
\par Abide in me, and they shall ever be;
\par Fulfil at once 
\par Thy precept and my prayer:
\par Come and abide in me,
\par  and I in Thee.
\par                                                   Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

